Z||000044||Phaeton||12-24-2000||05:18 PM||||Lurch to the left, nose to the right.  <BR>This was after a new alignment  Turned out the rear camber was off almost a degree positive.  Before that happened I would have staked large amounts on the belief that one degree wouldn't matter.  Seems the tiny details are hidden gremlins causing a lot of seemingly big problems.<P>Oh yeah, as long as information is put in along with the bickering then it's all still good.||||reg||12
Z||000045||Standard||12-25-2000||04:54 AM||||Not trying to continue the flames, just wondering..<P>Why can't the Fiero torque steer?  It <B>is</B> basically a FWD setup mounted in the rear.. I've noticed the same thing, and quick shift to the left between shifts when I'm accelerating hard...  darned if I'm wrong, but it seems as thought the <B>torque</B> is <B>steering</B> the car a bit...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
